    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The only test class (`AcceptanceTest`) passes and the build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nA single line in `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 the `registrationDate` property of the `OwnerFields` schema now carries a generator vendor extension:\n\n```yaml\nx-field-extra-annotation: '@jakarta.validation.constraints.PastOrPresent'\n```\n\n## Why this way\n\n- The generated `OwnerFieldsDto` field picks up `@PastOrPresent`, and the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` already binds the body with `@Valid @RequestBody`. A supplied `registrationDate` after the server date now fails bean validation, which Spring's existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` turns into a **400** automatically (confirmed in the logs: `Validation error at POST /api/owners \u2026 must be a date in the past or in the present`).\n- **Zero structural cost.** I edited no functions and no classes \u2014 just the spec. The `cost = WMC_other * CC * changed_lines` sum is over changed functions, of which there are none. Notably I avoided touching the large, high-complexity `addOwner` controller method, which would have been the expensive place to add a manual check.\n- It's the idiomatic Spring path: declarative Bean Validation on the request DTO rather than imperative date-comparison logic, and it reuses the app's existing validation-to-400 error handling.\n\nOmitted (absent `registrationDate`) still defaults to the server date as before, since `@PastOrPresent` permits null.",
